<DocsPage id="verified-completion">

          <p>
            Completion you can check, instead of a confident summary. Turn on LLM-as-a-judge and finishing stops
            being the agent's own opinion. Before it starts, the agent writes down the observable success criteria
            your request implies. After implementing, it has to exercise the work rather than describe it. Then the
            Judge, a read-only <a href="/docs/subagents#specialists">subagent specialist</a>, compares the original
            request, the criteria, the changed files and the captured test output. A FAIL names the specific repair and
            sends the agent back to work, up to three rounds.
          </p>
          <p class="note">
            Opt-in, and it spends extra model calls on every prompt it covers. It cannot apply to the plan lane, which
            produces nothing to verify, or to the quick lane, which has no ability to spawn the judge at all.
          </p>
</DocsPage>
